                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Ubinota is a puzzle game that focuses on logic, problem-solving, and carefully planning your moves. The game challenges players to think ahead and find solutions using its unique mechanics rather than relying on speed or reflexes.\n\nThe biggest strength of Ubinota is its puzzle design. The game encourages players to experiment, analyse situations, and figure out the correct approach. Solving a difficult puzzle can feel rewarding because success comes from understanding the mechanics rather than simply trying again.\n\nThe gameplay is simple to learn but can become increasingly challenging. This balance helps make the game accessible while still giving puzzle fans something to think about. The focus on logic makes it a good choice for players who enjoy slower, more thoughtful experiences.\n\nThe presentation supports the puzzle-focused design. By keeping attention on the mechanics and challenges, the game avoids unnecessary distractions and lets the player focus on solving problems.\n\nHowever, the biggest weakness is that puzzle games can be very dependent on personal taste. Players who enjoy logic challenges may find it engaging, but those looking for action, story, or more variety may find the experience too focused.\n\nThe difficulty curve can also be a mixed point. Some puzzles may feel satisfying when solved, while others may become frustrating if the solution is unclear or requires a very specific way of thinking.\n\nReplay value depends on how much you enjoy solving puzzles. Once the challenges are completed, there may not be much reason to return unless you want to replay levels or improve your understanding of the mechanics.\n\nOverall, Ubinota is a solid puzzle game with a focus on logic and creative problem-solving. It provides a satisfying challenge for puzzle fans, but its narrow focus means it may not appeal to players who prefer more varied gameplay experiences.\n\nRating: 7/10\n",
